      "transcriber_notes": [
        "Table printed sideways (rotated); read from rotated crops.",
        "Multi-line Armament entries joined with '; '.",
        "Rows Chiang Ling, Chiang Li, Chiang Tsing: a single line of text '1-12 c. 1-3″, 4-3 pdr. 4 Maxims' is printed across the Displacement/Draught/Date Launched columns, with no Length, Displacement, Draught, Date or Knots figures; placed in Armament here, cells for those columns left blank as printed (not unreadable).",
        "Row Chiangyuan Armament: the lines '1-3″', '4-1 pdr.', '9 Machine' run on in the Armament column below Chiangyuan's '1-12 pdr.', level with the Chiang Ling/Li/Tsing rows; those three ships have their own armament printed in-line across the Displacement–Date columns, and on this page each ship's first armament line is level with its name, so the lines are Chiangyuan's.",
        "Row Chiangkun Knots: printed ':2' — only a serif fleck and a bottom dot survive of the first digit (probably 1, i.e. 12, but not legible); blank. Row Chiangchung Knots '11': first 1 broken ('!1') but the stroke runs nearly full height; read with certainty. Row Chiangyuan Knots '12': top of the first 1 broken, upper stroke with serif clearly a 1.",
        "Chinese name of Chiang Ling printed as 江 + a 甯/寗-type variant character; rendered 江甯.",
        "Running head: THE CHINESE NAVY, Ch. XVIII.",
        "Check pass C06: knots and armament re-read from rotated full-resolution crops with pixel zooms of the broken digits; armament assignments confirmed; changed: Chiangkun Knots 12→\"\" (first digit not legible)."
