      "transcriber_notes": [
        "Table printed sideways (rotated) on p1135 (p. 764) and continued as 'Training Squadron.—(Continued).' on p1136 (p. 765); rows merged. Rows from Pu An onward are on p. 765.",
        "Multi-line cells joined with '; ' (Armament) or a space.",
        "Draught ',,' = ditto marks as printed.",
        "Unnamed row after Teh Shen: a line reading '—' (Date Launched) and '2 Maxims.' (Armament) is printed on its own between Teh Shen and Yi Shen, with no name; kept as a separate row with empty stub. It may belong to Yi Shen, whose Date Launched cell is otherwise empty.",
        "Row Yung Shen Displacement: empty as printed (not unreadable). Rows Chin Shen, Jing Shen, Fu Ting Armament: empty as printed. Chin Shen and Jing Shen printed without Chinese characters.",
        "Row Fu Ting Location printed as a short double dash '--'.",
        "Rows Pu An / Kan Chuan: Armament '1-3″' is level with Pu An; '4-1 pdr.' is level with Kan Chuan and '2-12 mm.' follows below it, so Pu An = '1-3″', Kan Chuan = '4-1 pdr.; 2-12 mm.' (first line of each ship's armament is level with its name throughout these pages). Kan Chuan Draught cell reads 'Launched :' as printed (the date 1909 follows in the next column); Kan Chuan Knots empty as printed.",
        "Rows Wei Sung, Yi Sung, Wu Sung, Sui Sung: bracketed together with the single entry 'Small gunboats for river duty mounting Maxims and quickfirers.' spanning the table; placed in Type for each.",
        "Row Ming Chuen: '(Keel laid Jan. 16, 1929, Kiangnan to be completed in 11 months)' printed on a line below the row, placed in Type. Draught: smudged/illegible glyphs (perhaps ending in 3′) — left blank. Date Launched: a smudged dash, transcribed '—'.",
        "Rows Wei Sing / Teh Sing: bracketed together with the two-line entry 'To be converted to aircraft tenders. Upper deck cut away. / Two seaplanes aft. One four inch gun forward.' placed in Type for each.",
        "Running head: THE CHINESE NAVY, Ch. XVIII.",
        "Check pass C06: p. 764 lower block and p. 765 re-read from rotated full-resolution crops; the stray line '— / 2 Maxims.' between Teh Shen and Yi Shen stands on its own line with no name (kept as its own row; its owner cannot be told from the layout); Ming Chuen Draught remains a smudge (blank); no changes."
      ],
